This NOTICE records third-party work that CutoutML reimplements, redistributes at
runtime, or depends on. It exists because the licence of a *model* is not the licence of
its *weights*, and because two of the weight files this project can download carry terms
that differ from this repository's. A full discussion is in docs/models.md and
docs/licensing.md; this file is the short, authoritative attribution list.

No model weights are committed to this repository. Everything below describes artefacts
that are either produced locally by `make weights` or fetched on demand by
`python -m cutoutml.models.download_weights`.

================================================================================
1. Architectures reimplemented in this repository
================================================================================

U^2-Net
  Paper:    Qin, Zhang, Huang, Dehghan, Zaiane, Jagersand,
            "U^2-Net: Going Deeper with Nested U-Structure for Salient Object
            Detection", Pattern Recognition 106 (2020).
  Upstream: https://github.com/xuebinqin/U-2-Net
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0

  src/cutoutml/models/u2net/arch.py is an independent implementation written from the
  paper, not a copy of the upstream source. It is deliberately shape-compatible with the
  published checkpoints, and this repository redistributes no upstream code.

BiRefNet
  Paper:    Zheng, Peng et al., "Bilateral Reference for High-Resolution Dichotomous
            Image Segmentation", CAAI AIR 2024.
  Upstream: https://github.com/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet
  Licence:  MIT (upstream code)

  src/cutoutml/models/birefnet/ is architecture-inspired rather than a port, and is NOT
  weight-compatible with the official checkpoints. See section 3 for the warning that
  matters here.

GrabCut
  Paper:    Rother, Kolmogorov, Blake, "GrabCut: interactive foreground extraction using
            iterated graph cuts", SIGGRAPH 2004.
  Implementation: OpenCV's cv2.grabCut (Apache License 2.0). The seeding, trimap
  construction and post-processing in this repository are original.

Spectral-residual saliency
  Paper:    Hou & Zhang, "Saliency Detection: A Spectral Residual Approach", CVPR 2007.
  Implemented here directly on NumPy/OpenCV FFT primitives.

CutoutNet
  Original to this repository. Architecture and weights are MIT, and are not derived from
  any pretrained model.

================================================================================
2. Pretrained weights this project can download
================================================================================

u2net.onnx, u2netp.onnx
  Content:  The U^2-Net authors' published weights, exported to ONNX with the
            BatchNorm layers folded into their preceding convolutions.
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0, inherited from the upstream weights.
  Obtained: https://github.com/danielgatis/rembg/releases/download/v0.0.0/
            The rembg project (MIT) redistributes these files; the weights themselves
            originate from https://github.com/xuebinqin/U-2-Net, whose authors
            distribute them via Google Drive.
  SHA-256:  u2net.onnx   8d10d2f3bb75ae3b6d527c77944fc5e7dcd94b29809d47a739a7a728a912b491
            u2netp.onnx  309c8469258dda742793dce0ebea8e6dd393174f89934733ecc8b14c76f4ddd8
            Both digests are pinned in src/cutoutml/models/download_weights.py and
            verified on download.

u2net.pt, u2netp.pt
  Content:  Derived from the two ONNX graphs above by
            cutoutml.models.u2net.from_onnx, which extracts the folded convolution
            weights and neutralises the BatchNorm layers. Numerically equivalent to the
            source graph to within 1.4e-7 (full) and 1.5e-6 (lite), verified against
            onnxruntime at conversion time.
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0. A format conversion does not change the licence of the
            weights, and each converted file carries its provenance and licence inside
            it rather than in a sidecar that can be separated from the weights.

u2net.pth, u2netp.pth (optional alternative route)
  Content:  The authors' original PyTorch checkpoints.
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0.
  Obtained: HuggingFace mirrors, which are blocked in some networks including the one
            this repository was developed in.

================================================================================
3. Weights this project deliberately does NOT download
================================================================================

BiRefNet checkpoints
  The official BiRefNet code is MIT, but SOME third-party fine-tuned BiRefNet
  checkpoints are published under non-commercial terms. Anyone using a BiRefNet
  checkpoint obtained from a third party is responsible for reading that specific
  file's licence; "BiRefNet is MIT" is true of the code and not necessarily of the
  weights.

  This repository ships none, offers no download URL for them, and its BiRefNet
  reimplementation is not weight-compatible with them in any case - so no
  non-commercial artefact can arrive here by accident.

